  "body": "Just a few leisurely steps from the sand, this stylish north facing gem one street back from the waterfront has been fully renovated. The coastal bolthole boasts attributes on many a wish list and will have broad appeal for those seeking a retreat from the hurry-scurry of the big city. Comprising of a practical leasehold title, the property is well positioned for abundant sun on the ground floor of a four-unit 1970s-built complex. \r\n \r\nA sophisticated, neutral decor complements the refurbished 100 sqm (approx.) interior which incorporates floor plan layout with direct connection to discretely allocated outdoor zones. Generously proportioned open plan living and dining areas with wall mounted heat pump enjoy seamless flow to the alfresco patio, flat, fenced lawns and established gardens. This is a sheltered and restful spot to entertain friends and gather them around the barbecue come summer. Whip up all the culinary delights your heart desires in the superbly designed kitchen with freestanding island where stainless steel appliances fit neatly with floor to ceiling flush cabinetry and extensive composite stone benchtops. The king-sized double bedroom has built in closets while an adjacent fully tiled bathroom boasts dual basins, bold, claret-red cabinetry and chrome fittings. The unit comes with hideaway laundry in the hall while the single garage has an extra carpark on the forecourt. \r\n \r\nIn zone for top schools and close to cafes, boutiques, bars and restaurants, while public transport and main arterial routes are super handy for commuters heading into the city centre. Bringing together soul-soothing green spaces with the benefits of proximity to upmarket cosmopolitan precincts, this coastal cocoon is an ideal base for busy professionals, globetrotting retirees, beach-loving downsizers, and discerning investors.\r\n\r\nThis is a leasehold property with total annual outgoings of $47,624.30, including the ground lease ($41,875.00 p.a.), council rates ($4,102.47 p.a.), and insurance ($1,646.83 p.a.).",
